          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: 3f6fc46dd5f94ef654b685b11fbb64f0700bb78e8da3dba9fcb55525915202d0\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: e0dd8c7bf54a46474d09cc23186d5a7c12d883421d2c187fc8025d4ddbf0297f\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "Configure storm control for each host-facing interface as shown in the example below:\n\nSW1(config)#int range g0/2 - 8 \nSW1(config-if-range)#storm-control unicast bps 62000000 \nSW1(config-if-range)#storm-control broadcast level bps 20000000 \n\nNote: The acceptable range is 10000000 -1000000000 for a gigabit Ethernet interface, and 100000000-10000000000 for a ten gigabit interface. Storm control is not supported on most FastEthernet interfaces.",
